 ## Background
-Neural Harmonic Textures (NHT) is a primitive-based neural representation that increases the expressive power of individual primitives by anchoring latent feature vectors on a virtual scaffold around each primitive, applying periodic activations to interpolated features, and decoding the accumulated signal via a single deferred MLP pass [Parent]. The 2D adaptation was introduced to handle high-resolution image fitting by replacing 3D primitives with a 2D mesh and modifying the interpolation scheme [S1]. The method is compatible with deferred-shading rendering pipelines [S1].
+Neural Harmonic Textures is a primitive-based neural representation that increases the expressive power of individual primitives by anchoring latent feature vectors on a virtual scaffold around each primitive, applying periodic activations to interpolated features, and decoding the accumulated signal via a single deferred MLP pass [Parent]. The 2D adaptation was introduced to handle high-resolution image fitting by replacing 3D primitives with a 2D mesh and modifying the interpolation scheme [S1]. The method is compatible with deferred-shading rendering pipelines [S1].
 
